      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tree body (cone)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Start at the tip. Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-tree"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and work 4 dc into the ring. Do not join. Place a stitch marker. Work in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "continuous-rounds-tree"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "continuous rounds"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", increasing every second stitch each round. Continue until the base measures 10 cm across, then stuff firmly and close."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the last round, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-tree"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " around to 6 stitches. Stuff the piece before the gap gets too small. Use an "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "invisible-join-tree"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "invisible fasten-off"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to close. Weave in the end."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Trunk (cylinder)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a small cylinder 2 cm tall and 2 cm wide using brown yarn. Stuff lightly. Sew centred to the base of the tree cone using ladder stitch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Baubles (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work four small spheres each 2 cm across in red yarn. Stuff firmly. Sew evenly around the cone surface using the tail."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 6 in yellow yarn, join into a loop, and sew to the tip of the tree as a star. Weave in all ends. The tree can be lightly misted and shaped while damp if it lists to one side."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
